# LOB — UI / UX chrome

Apply when editing shell layout, brand marks, nav, or page chrome. Prefer existing brand components over new ad-hoc logos.

## Brand hierarchy (do not stack duplicates)

| Layer | Component | Role |
|-------|-----------|------|
| Global wordmark | `LobBrandMasthead` in `src/app/layout.tsx` | Sole full-bleed top brand bar |
| Primary nav | `AppNav` | Links + auth only — **no** LOB mark / wood-O |
| In-app sidebar | `LobSidebar` | Text only: product name + positioning — **no** LOB mark |
| Status chrome | `RoleRibbon`, `AdminViewAsBar`, `DemoBanner` | Role/admin/demo — not brand logos |

- **One global masthead** — do not add a second wordmark above/beside `AppNav`.
- **Masthead lockup** — dark navy bar (`bg-lob-navy`) with the **knockout** LOB letters (`LOB_APP_ICON_KNOCKOUT_SRC`, no navy box) to the **left** of a **vector** “Lumber One Board” wordmark (white + gold “One”, Nunito 800). No `#1` tagline. Do not use the boxed `lob-app-icon.png` on the navy bar — the field color does not match.
- **Masthead is full-bleed** — `w-full` edge-to-edge; do not re-introduce `max-w-[1680px]` on the masthead shell (content pages may still use that max width).
- **No logo in `AppNav` or `LobSidebar`** — the square mark lives in the masthead only.
- Reuse `@/components/lob-brand-*`, `LobWoodOIcon`, `@/lib/brand`, `@/lib/brand-marketing` — do not invent new lockups.

## UX defaults

- Match neighboring Tailwind patterns (stone/navy/gold tokens in `globals.css`).
- Preserve persona body tints (`PersonaBodyTint`) — do not override with one-off page backgrounds unless the task asks.
- Mobile: same centered lockup at a smaller size; do not force a second brand treatment on phones.
- Minimal diffs — no drive-by redesign of unrelated surfaces.

## Ship

- UI/UX session changes land on **`origin/main`** (commit + push) so the existing Vercel project **`lob`** deploys — do not create a new Vercel project.
- Production aliases: `lob-damian-les-projects.vercel.app` (and related). Per-deploy `lob-*-damian-les-projects.vercel.app` URLs are snapshots of that same project.

## Entry points

- Shell: `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/components/app-nav.tsx`, `src/components/lob-brand-masthead.tsx`
- Workspace chrome: `src/components/lob-sidebar.tsx`, `src/components/load-board-workspace.tsx`
- Tokens: `src/app/globals.css`, `src/lib/brand.ts`
